<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

Rich, interactive content floating beside a control - a form, settings, a share sheet.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/popover)

<%= embed UI::PopoverPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Popover do
  PopoverTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Share" } }
  PopoverContent do
    PopoverTitle { "Share this page" }
    PopoverDescription { "Anyone with the link can view this document." }
  end
end
```

The popup opens in the browser's top layer (no `overflow` clips it) on click, placed by `side:` / `align:` on
PopoverContent with an arrow pointing at the trigger, and flips or shifts to stay in view. Focus moves into it; Escape,
a click outside or a `PopoverClose` dismiss it and return focus. `PopoverTrigger(open_on_hover: true)` also opens it
on pointer rest. For a list of actions use a [Dropdown Menu](<%= page_path(:dropdown_menu) %>); for a short hint, a
[Tooltip](<%= page_path(:tooltip) %>).

